Spec: LibStorageClassSelector

Platform: Rhai script library (vynil-core 0.7.7 engine)

Purpose:
  Pick the one StorageClass entry a workload family should use — singleton PVC, deployment
    shared volume, statefulset volume, or VM disk — by walking a fixed preference chain over
    @context.cluster.prefered_storage of the enriched class list and falling back to the
    cluster default class. Pure read-only selectors over the `cluster.storage_classes` /
    `cluster.prefered_storage` shape ./build_context.rhai mounts; no cluster access of its own.

Exposes:
  @for_singletons(context, typed) / @for_singletons(context) — RWO-shaped chain; the
    1-arity overload forwards @typed = `()`.
  @for_deployments(context, typed) / @for_deployments(context) — RWX-first chain; 1-arity
    overload forwards `()`.
  @for_statefulsets(context, typed) / @for_statefulsets(context) — RWO-only chain; 1-arity
    overload forwards `()`.
  @for_vm(context) — Block-mode chain; deliberately no typed overload.
  All seven top-level fns are importable; the only import in the repo is
    `import "storage_class_selector" as sel` in ./../../tests/rhai_lib.rs — no shipped
    .rhai/.hbs calls these fns (Tasks).

Accepts:
  @context — map read as @context.cluster.storage_classes (Array of enriched entries; the
    predicates read @name, @volumeMode, @is_default) and @context.cluster.prefered_storage
    (map with the keys @get_prefered_sc writes, per ./storage_class_enrich.sdd). Missing
    keys inside a present map read as `()`; absent @cluster / @prefered_storage maps or a
    non-array @storage_classes raise (Raises).
  @typed — optional @String; only `"fast"` and `"cheap"` carry meaning. Any other value —
    including the wrappers' `()` — behaves as untyped: `() == "fast"` is false. Never validated.

Returns:
  The matched ENTRY MAP — the whole enriched `#{name, provisioner, volumeMode, ...}` entry,
    not just @name (callers index @name themselves) — or `()` on any rhai @find miss.
    Absence NEVER throws: empty list, unmatched arm, or no @is_default hit all yield `()`;
    a caller's `.name` on the unit is the error site.
  Fallback asymmetry: the else arm's predicate is @is_default alone — no @volumeMode guard —
    so @for_vm's fallback can surface a `"Filesystem"` default although its block arms
    require `"Block"`.

Raises:
  Zero @throw and zero @try in these 68 lines; the only raises are rhai engine errors
    escaping tolerant reads: dereferencing a property of `()` when @cluster or
    @cluster.prefered_storage is absent (the FIRST chain guard already dereferences
    @prefered_storage, so even an all-unit run needs it present), or @find on a non-array.
    Name mismatches and wrong @volumeMode are plain false predicates, never errors.

Handles:
  `storage_classes: []` with any preference set → `()`: the guarded arm is selected by the
    key check, its @find simply misses (test-pinned).
  A set preference whose entry is absent or has the wrong @volumeMode → the if/else chain
    selects an arm by the `!= ()` guard, NOT by find success → returns `()` and later
    preferences are never consulted.
  Un-enriched entries (no @volumeMode key): reads `()`, never equals `"Filesystem"`/`"Block"`
    → every preference arm misses → @is_default decides regardless of the class's real mode.
  Missing/non-boolean @is_default — taken as never-matching, the @pick_sc posture frozen for
    the same engine in ./storage_class_enrich.sdd; not probed on this lane (Tasks).

Must:
  The chain order IS the algorithm; first `!= ()`-guard hit wins and consumes the chain.
    `[fast]`/`[cheap]` mark arms that additionally require @typed to equal that literal.
    Every preference arm's predicate is `s.name == <key> && s.volumeMode == "Filesystem"`
    (`for_vm` arms: `"Block"`); all keys are under @cluster.prefered_storage:
    - @for_singletons: `distibuted_readWriteOnce` → [fast] `fs_fast_readWriteOnce` →
      [cheap] `fs_cheap_readWriteOnce` → `fs_readWriteOnce` → @is_default.
    - @for_deployments: [fast] `fs_fast_readWriteMany` → [cheap] `fs_cheap_readWriteMany` →
      `fs_readWriteMany` → [fast] `fs_fast_readWriteOnce` → [cheap]
      `fs_cheap_readWriteOnce` → `distibuted_readWriteOnce` → `fs_readWriteOnce` →
      @is_default.
    - @for_statefulsets: [fast] `fs_fast_readWriteOnce` → [cheap] `fs_cheap_readWriteOnce`
      → `fs_readWriteOnce` → @is_default; reads no readWriteMany nor distributed key at all.
    - @for_vm: `block_readWriteMany` → `block_readWriteOnce` → @is_default.
  In @for_singletons the `distibuted_readWriteOnce` arm PRECEDES the typed arms — a
    `"fast"` singleton still gets the distributed class; in @for_deployments all three RWX
    arms outrank everything RWO below them.
  The if/else chain is the function value: rhai returns the taken branch's @find result as
    the fn result; the three 1-arity wrappers delegate with `()`, so the fast/cheap arms
    cannot match through them even if the keys were populated.
  Key names are read verbatim, misspellings included: `distibuted_readWriteOnce` and
    `prefered_storage` are the frozen contract of ./storage_class_enrich.sdd and
    ./build_context.rhai, not to be normalized here.
  Zero side effects, zero engine-API calls: import-time code is nil (fn declarations only),
    no @k8s_resource/@throw/@log; all data arrives via @context and is never mutated.
  The fast/cheap arms (file lines 5-8, 21-24, 27-30, 45-48) are unreachable as shipped —
    @get_prefered_sc never writes `fs_cheap_*`/`fs_fast_*` (frozen in
    ./storage_class_enrich.sdd Must), the only callers (tests) use the 1-arity wrappers,
    and the sole other lane is a hand-written `agent.yaml` preference map past
    ./build_context.rhai's injection guard — no shipped config sets those keys (Tasks,
    decision shared with the producer's open item).

Depends on:
  rhai std only — @find, `==`, and the tolerant map-miss-to-unit semantics frozen in
    ./build_context.sdd; zero vynil-core registrations are reached.
  ./storage_class_enrich.sdd — upstream producer of the entry shape (@volumeMode,
    @is_default) and of the preference map; its never-written cheap/fast slots define this
    file's dead arms.
  ./build_context.sdd — the @template/@run lanes mounting the two keys under @cluster and
    the agent.yaml lane that could substitute a hand-authored preference map (the only
    route that could revive the typed arms).

Scenario: distributed preference resolves a singleton volume
  Given storage_classes [local-path FS, ceph-distributed FS], distibuted_readWriteOnce
    = "ceph-distributed", every other preference key `()`
  When @for_singletons(context) runs
  Then the ceph-distributed entry map is returned (test-pinned in ./../../tests/rhai_lib.rs)

Scenario: empty class list yields unit, not error
  Given storage_classes [] and distibuted_readWriteOnce = "ceph-distributed"
  When @for_singletons(context) runs
  Then the distributed arm is selected, its @find misses, and `()` is returned without a
    raise (test-pinned)

Scenario: set preference with a missing entry starves later preferences
  Given distibuted_readWriteOnce = "gone" (no such @name in the list) and
    `fs_readWriteOnce` = "local-path" (present, `"Filesystem"`)
  When @for_singletons(context) runs
  Then `()` is returned — the chain was consumed by the first `!= ()` guard and
    `fs_readWriteOnce` is never consulted

Scenario: deployments fall through RWX to the RWO preference
  Given all readWriteMany keys `()`, `fs_readWriteOnce` = "ceph-rwo" with that entry
    present as `"Filesystem"`
  When @for_deployments(context) runs
  Then the ceph-rwo entry is returned (test-pinned)

Scenario: vm fallback ignores volumeMode
  Given `block_readWriteMany` and `block_readWriteOnce` both `()` and the only default
    entry carrying @volumeMode `"Filesystem"`
  When @for_vm(context) runs
  Then that Filesystem default entry is returned — the fallback predicate is @is_default
    alone

Tasks:
  [ ] Extend ./../../tests/rhai_lib.rs to the unpinned surface: @for_vm, @for_statefulsets,
      2-arity typed calls, the wrong-mode/missing-entry `()` arm-consumption case, and the
      missing-@is_default fallback posture.
  [?] The fast/cheap arms are dead as shipped (producer never writes the keys, no caller
      passes @typed): decide jointly with ./storage_class_enrich.sdd's matching `[?]` —
      populate the slots from some signal, or drop the four arms and the keys together.
  [?] Chain-order intent: for_singletons ranks distributed above fast/cheap,
      for_deployments ranks RWX above typed-RWO, for_statefulsets ignores readWriteMany and
      distributed entirely — confirm these are the deliberate family semantics.
  [?] No shipped consumer exists (repo grep: only ./../../tests/rhai_lib.rs imports it); a
      tier-2 toolkit asset like ./apps.rhai or ./gen_package.rhai. Also
      /docs/packages/lifecycle.md still names a non-existent `storage_class.rhai`. Decide
      wire-up target or removal, stale doc name included.

Done when:
  Every chain and the `()`-on-miss posture above has a green mock-engine test on the
    ./../../tests/rhai_lib.rs harness and the fast/cheap decision is recorded jointly with
    ./storage_class_enrich.sdd.
